description:
We are currently seeking a skilled and experienced
 **Data Scientist** 
 to join our team. As a Data Scientist, you will be responsible for experiments with datasets searching for useful insights and features, maintaining data pipelines and training machine learning algorithms, and visualizing results.




 Main goals and responsibilities:




* Be a proactive team worker;
* Collaborate with the team to implement new features to support the growing data needs;
* Build, maintain, and deploy DS and ML pipelines, including data retrieval, preprocessing, feature engineering, training, and inferencing the models, analyzing and visualizing the results;
* Build, maintain and deploy LLM\-powered systems and agent pipelines, including prompt engineering, tool and API integration, memory and context management, inference orchestration, and evaluation of model outputs;
* Share knowledge with other teams on various data science or project\-related topics;
* Collaborate with the team to decide on which tools and strategies to use within specific scenarios.


 Required:




* English level upper intermediate\+;
* Good mathematical and statistical background, tensor calculus;
* Good knowledge of databases such as Postgres, MongoDB, and SQL;
* Python language including practical experience with Scikit\-learn, Numpy, Pandas, and Matplot libraries;
* Experience with gradient boosting algorithms (XGBoost or LightGBM);
* Familiarity with LLM orchestration tools (e.g., LangChain, LangGraph);
* Experience using or integrating with cloud LLM APIs (e.g., OpenAI, Claude, Amazon Bedrock, Vertex AI);
* Hands\-on experience with Retrieval\-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines and vector databases (e.g., pgvector, FAISS, Weaviate, Pinecone);
* Practical experience with prompt engineering techniques, agentic tools and workflows;
* At least 1 framework to build and train neural networks (TensorFlow/Keras, PyTorch), a good understanding of neural networks architectures, and how\-tos;
* Commercial experience with classic machine learning and deep learning, including NLP and CV models like Bert, Resnet;
* Practical skills in building en\-to\-end ML training pipelines (data load, preprocess, train, inference), as well as GitHub / GitLab CI/CD flows;
* Docker or Kubernetes platform;
* Work experience as a Data Scientist more than 2 years.


 Nice to have:




* Hands\-on experience with at least one major cloud platform (AWS, Azure, or GCP);
* Ability to work with Spark, Airflow.


 What we offer:




* Long\-term career stability with a competitive salary paid in USD.
* Conditions for steady career development.
* Development supported by dedicated mentors and a variety of programs focused on expertise and innovation.
* Private medical insurance provided after successful completion of the probationary period
* A well\-equipped and cozy office supports comfort and productivity across all project stages.
* Welcoming atmosphere and a friendly corporate culture.


 If you feel this opportunity resonates with you, apply now — we're looking forward to getting to know you!

**Build the global data backbone for AI and workforce intelligence as a Data Engineer at HeadFirst Group**


Do you want to build scalable data platforms that power AI, analytics and intelligent workforce solutions on a global scale? Are you excited by modern Databricks environments, cloud\-native engineering and the opportunity to help shape the future of AI\-enabled platforms?


As a Data Engineer within the Global Data \& AI Team of HeadFirst Group \& Impellam Group, you will play a key role in building and scaling the data backbone behind our international Workforce\-as\-a\-Service (WaaS) strategy. You will work on our internally developed Headless Data Architecture (HDA): a scalable, API\-first lakehouse platform built on Azure Databricks, Delta Lake and Unity Catalog. This platform supports analytics, AI workloads and intelligent workforce solutions across Europe, North America and APAC.


What makes this role unique? You are not joining a traditional data team focused only on reporting or ETL. You will help build a modern global data platform where data engineering, AI enablement and platform scalability come together. You will work with modern technologies, AI\-assisted development tooling and an international engineering team that is actively shaping the next generation of workforce intelligence.

**Your impact at HeadFirst Group**


As a Data Engineer, you are responsible for designing, building and optimising scalable and production\-ready data pipelines within our global lakehouse ecosystem. You help create scalable and reusable data products powering analytics, AI and operational intelligence. You will contribute directly to the further development of our Headless Data Architecture (HDA), where governance and scalability are embedded into every layer of the platform.


In this role, you collaborate closely with ML/AI Engineers, Platform Engineers, Cloud Engineers and stakeholders across Europe, the UK, the US and APAC. Together, you help shape a modern cloud data platform that enables teams to exchange, govern and leverage data efficiently. You will join a growing international engineering team with significant ownership over platform decisions, engineering standards and the future direction of the platform.

**What will you do?**


Design, build and maintain Bronze Silver* Gold medallion pipelines in Azure Databricks;
* Develop scalable ETL/ELT pipelines using PySpark, Delta Lake and Databricks\-native tooling;
* Build deployable data products using Lakeflow, Spark Declarative Pipelines and Databricks Asset Bundles (DABs);
* Implement reusable data contracts and scalable data product patterns;
* Manage Unity Catalog governance, lineage and access management;
* Contribute to vector search, semantic search and AI\-enabled retrieval capabilities;
* Work within a global multi\-lakehouse architecture, including Delta Sharing across regions;
* Collaborate with international engineering teams on platform scalability and data exchange;
* Participate in Git\-based development, CI/CD workflows and code reviews;
* Monitor platform health, observability and DataOps reliability;
* Work with AI\-assisted development tooling such as Claude Code and the Databricks AI Dev Kit.

**About HeadFirst Group**


HeadFirst Group is a leading international workforce solutions provider and the largest Managed Service Provider in the Netherlands. Every day, we connect thousands of professionals with organisations such as Rabobank, Vattenfall, government institutions and many other public and private sector clients.


Through technology, data\-driven insights and specialised expertise, we help organisations navigate an increasingly complex and rapidly changing labour market. Within our Global Data \& AI Team, we are building the foundation for a truly AI\-enabled and data\-driven organisation. You will join an ambitious international engineering environment where innovation, ownership and collaboration are central. We combine enterprise scale with modern engineering practices and continuously invest in cloud\-native technologies, AI capabilities and platform maturity.


This is an opportunity to work on a modern Databricks ecosystem with real international impact, while helping shape the future of data and AI within a global organisation.

 *We believe talent cannot always be captured in a checklist. Are you excited about the role, but do not meet every single requirement? We would still love to hear from you. Our recruitment process leaves room for different backgrounds, experiences and ways of working. Feel free to let us know what you need to perform at your best.*

* 3\+ years of hands\-on Databricks experience in production environments;
* Strong experience with Medallion Architecture, Apache Spark, PySpark and Delta Lake;
* Experience with Databricks SQL, Unity Catalog and large\-scale data engineering workloads;
* Familiarity with Lakeflow, Spark Declarative Pipelines and Databricks Asset Bundles (DABs);
* Strong SQL and Python skills;
* Experience with Git workflows, CI/CD and DataOps practices;
* Understanding of data contracts and scalable data product design;
* Familiarity with vector search, semantic search or AI\-oriented data workloads is a plus;
* Experience in global or multi\-lakehouse Databricks environments is a strong plus;
* Familiarity with Azure Synapse Analytics and SnapLogic;
* Strong communication skills and a pragmatic engineering mindset;
* Curiosity about AI\-native engineering and modern platform development.

**Ready to help shape the future of AI\-driven workforce intelligence?**


Apply today and become part of the Global Data \& AI Team at HeadFirst Group \& Impellam Group. Together, we are building the global data platform powering the next generation of workforce solutions.



Mobility budget or Lease car: No


Brand: HeadFirst Group

Job Summary :

Our corporate activities are growing rapidly, and we are currently seeking a full\-time, office\-based Data Engineer to join our AI team. This position will work on a team to accomplish tasks and projects that are instrumental to the company’s success. If you want an exciting career where you use your previous expertise and can develop and grow your career even further, then this is the opportunity for you.
Responsibilities :
* Utilize skills in handling of more unconventional data such as unstructured content from web\-based sites and varying content (documents, images etc) into different data lakes and with different software solutions (Snowflake, Azure, SQL, Python);
* Provide the handling of (and where needed training of) Large Language Models (LLMs) in the Extract, Transform, and Load (ETL) of large corpus of data into a data lake;
* Participate in the Natural Language Processing (NLP) extract of unstructured data into structured meta\-data through the use of tools such as Semantic understanding and meaning (Python, use of REST API);
* Support ensuring the data flow of any external content coming in is handled to the latest US and EU AI Acts concerning AI which includes security, confidentiality and privacy of PHI;
* Collect, analyze and document user requirements working with AI engineers to align data sources to downstream integration within systems;
* Create software applications that support the understanding and visualization of data flows from inception to derivation whilst maintaining version control by following software development lifecycle process, which includes requirements gathering, design, development, testing, release, and maintenance;
* Participate in software validation process through development, review, and/or execution of test plan/cases/scripts;
* Communicate with team members regarding projects, development, tools, and procedures; and
* Provide end\-user support including setup, installation, and maintenance for application


Qualifications :
* Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science, Data Science, or a related field;
* 1\-3\+ years of experience in Data Engineering;
* Background in working with AI tools that support areas such as data extraction and natural language processing and handling of varied unstructured content into structured meta\-data;
* Knowledge of developing dimensional data models from unstructured content and awareness of the advantages and limitations of Star Schema and Snowflake schema designs;
* Solid ETL development, reporting knowledge based off intricate understanding of business process and measures;
* Knowledge of Snowflake cloud data warehouse and Azure cloud is preferred;
* Knowledge of REST API;
* Good knowledge of SQL Server databases and Python programming language is required;
* Knowledge of C\# is a bonus as is working with Azure data fabric; and
* Excellent analytical, written and oral communication skills


Medpace Overview :

Medpace is a full\-service clinical contract research organization (CRO). We provide Phase I\-IV clinical development services to the biotechnology, pharmaceutical and medical device industries. Our mission is to accelerate the global development of safe and effective medical therapeutics through its scientific and disciplined approach. We leverage local regulatory and therapeutic expertise across all major areas including oncology, cardiology, metabolic disease, endocrinology, central nervous system, anti\-viral and anti\-infective. Headquartered in Cincinnati, Ohio, employing more than 6,000 people across 40\+ countries.
Why Medpace? :

People. Purpose. Passion. Make a Difference Tomorrow. Join Us Today.  

The work we’ve done over the past 30\+ years has positively impacted the lives of countless patients and families who face hundreds of diseases across all key therapeutic areas. The work we do today will improve the lives of people living with illness and disease in the future. **Medpace Perks**

* Flexible work environment
* Competitive compensation and benefits package
* Competitive PTO packages
* Structured career paths with opportunities for professional growth
* Company\-sponsored employee appreciation events
* Employee health and wellness initiatives

**Awards*** Recognized by Forbes as one of America's Most Successful Midsize Companies in 2021, 2022, 2023 and 2024
* Continually recognized with CRO Leadership Awards from Life Science Leader magazine based on expertise, quality, capabilities, reliability, and compatibility

 **What to Expect Next**
A Medpace team member will review your qualifications and, if interested, you will be contacted with details for next steps.

**Your mission**
 Robots couldn’t handle soft materials. We fixed that.




 Now we’re scaling it into reality, and we need someone who can make the impossible
 *reliable.*
 At sewts, we build the intelligence that lets robots manipulate deformable materials like textiles, towels, cables with human\-like precision. Our systems are already deployed in production across Europe and expanding into the US.




 We are building a foundational technology stack called sewts.JUPITER. JUPITER uses genAI to simulate realistically the behavior of deformable \& soft objects to create corresponding computer vision models and grabbing strategies. Based on our physical AI, for the first time ever, robots are enabled to handle soft \& deformable materials. With over €10M in funding we will bring automation into all untapped industries, like cloth manufacturing, textiles handling, recycling \& e\-commerce.




 This is where AI leaves the screen and enters the physical world.




 And in the physical world, nothing forgives you.




 You make Physical AI work in reality.




 Not on paper. Not in demos. Not in ideal conditions but with industrial required speed.




 Gripping of deformable materials like textiles is a task most humans see as intuitive and simple.




 However, this is a complicated task for robots as they lack the detailed and contextual understanding of where and with what level of sensitivity to handle these textiles.




**What You’ll Actually Do**
* Build and scale AI systems that run on real robots in real environments;
* Develop deep learning models (Python, PyTorch) for computer vision and manipulation;
* Design and maintain end\-to\-end ML pipelines (training → evaluation → deployment);
* Own experiment tracking, reproducibility, and model lifecycle discipline;
* Push model performance toward robustness under real\-world noise and edge cases;
* Automate training workflows, hyperparameter optimisation, and model iteration loops;
* Work tightly with robotics,MLOps, and simulation teams;
* Help shape sewts.JUPITER into a production\-grade Physical AI platform.


**Your profile**
**Who You Are**
* 2\-4 years' work experience in computer vision applications (object detection, classification);
* Strong Python and PyTorch fundamentals;
* Experienced with ClearML, GCP, or similar ML infrastructure stacks;
* Deep understanding of model training, evaluation, and failure modes;
* Experience with ML pipelines, cloud infrastructure, or MLOps tooling;
* You care about what survives contact with reality, not just what looks good in experiments;
* You move fast, think clearly, and fix things when they break;
* You’re comfortable operating without perfect structure;
* You are fluent in English.


**Nice to Have**
* Experience with robotics, industrial AI, or embodied systems;
* Vision Language Models or scene understanding exposure;
* Model optimization (TensorRT, quantization, PTQ);
* Experience in productionizing machine learning solutions.


**Why us?**
**Why This Role**
* You build AI that physically acts in the world—not just predicts it;
* Your work runs directly on deployed robotic systems;
* Small team, extreme ownership, no abstraction layers;
* You shape a category: Physical AI for deformable materials;
* Real impact is visible in production, not dashboards;
* Munich\-based, high\-performance environment.


**Setup \& Benefits**
* Competitive salary \+ VSOP participation;
* Learning budget \+ fast growth environment;
* Deutschlandticket \+ EGYM Wellpass;
* Speciality coffee at the office;
* Flexible working setup;
* Regular team events, high trust, low bureaucracy.


**Reality Check**
 Things will break. Edge cases will win.




 If you want clean problems, this is not it. If you want to build intelligence that survives the real world—
 **welcome to sewts.**
**Your Talent Partner**
 We want to ensure a smooth recruitment process for you. If you have questions or would like to know more about this role, your Talent Partner, Fatima, is there to support you.








 You may use the following channels to connect with her:








 Email: fatima.sakhawat@sewts.de




 WhatsApp: \+49 1577 74 44 352




**About Us**
 At sewts we are automating complex processes by teaching robots human\-like perception skills. We are a young, ambitious, and diverse team of eight different nationalities with the mission to become the global go\-to Partner for automated processing of deformable and soft materials. We are always willing to push our boundaries to reach our goals and targets, while learning from the daily challenges of an emerging startup. We are always on a hunt for likeminded individuals who are passionate about robotics automation, AI and courageous to create an impact. Are you ready?

Description




 Relevant du Gestionnaire, Analytique e‑commerce \& Expérimentation, l’Analyste en expérimentation analytique \& CRO sera responsable de la conception et de l’exécution du programme d’expérimentation sur les expériences web et mobile de Groupe Dynamite pour les marques Garage et Dynamite.




 Ce rôle consiste à définir la stratégieDescription




 Relevant du Gestionnaire, Analytique e‑commerce et Expérimentation, l’Analyste en Expérimentation \& CRO sera responsable de la gestion et de l’exécution du programme d’expérimentation sur les expériences web et mobile de Groupe Dynamite pour les marques Garage et Dynamite.




 Ce rôle consiste à définir la stratégie d’expérimentation, construire et prioriser la feuille de route des tests, lancer des tests A/B, analyser les résultats avec rigueur statistique et transformer les insights en impact mesurable sur la conversion et les revenus. L’analyste collaborera étroitement avec les équipes produit, développement, QA, marketing et eCommerce, et agira à titre d’expert des meilleures pratiques en expérimentation et CRO.




 Feuille de route et stratégie d’expérimentation




* Être responsable de la feuille de route d’expérimentation web et mobile pour les deux marques, alignée avec les objectifs trimestriels de conversion et de revenus;
* Identifier de manière proactive des opportunités d’amélioration incrémentale sur l’ensemble du funnel : engagement, découverte produit, ajout au panier, initiation du paiement et post‑achat;
* Générer des hypothèses créatives et basées sur les données issues de la recherche UX, des enregistrements de sessions, de l’analyse de funnel et des comportements clients;
* Prioriser les tests à l’aide d’un cadre structuré de scoring et s’assurer que la roadmap reflète en permanence les opportunités à plus fort impact.


 Planification et mise en place des tests




* Rédiger des tickets Jira détaillés pour chaque expérimentation incluant : hypothèse, brief de test, critères d’acceptation, métriques de succès, définition de l’audience et cas limites;
* Définir les métriques principales et de contrôle pour chaque test et configurer les segments d’audience dans SiteSpect et Optimizely;
* Implémenter les tests web en collaboration avec les développeurs et coordonner les tests applicatifs avec les équipes produit et développement;
* Maintenir un processus documenté étape par étape pour assurer une exécution cohérente et reproductible selon les parties prenantes et types de tests.


 Coordination et communication




* Animer des réunions mensuelles d’alignement avec les équipes produit, design, marketing et marque;
* Gérer la communication de bout en bout pour chaque test : liens de staging, mises à jour d’implémentation, validation QA et confirmations de mise en production;
* Informer de manière proactive les parties prenantes sur l’état des tests, les résultats et les prochaines étapes.


 QA, UAT et lancement




* Diriger le processus QA pour chaque test avant mise en ligne, incluant appareils, navigateurs et cas limites;
* Gérer les phases UAT et obtenir les validations nécessaires avant lancement;
* Lancer les tests dans SiteSpect et Optimizely et gérer le processus de mise en production de A à Z.


 Suivi, analyse et résultats




* Surveiller en continu les tests en cours et signaler immédiatement toute anomalie ou problème technique;
* Effectuer l’analyse statistique des résultats : significativité, intervalles de confiance, analyses par segment et modélisation de l’impact sur les revenus;
* Déclarer les résultats selon un seuil minimal de 95 % de confiance — sans jamais conclure prématurément;
* Produire une documentation claire dans Confluence ainsi que des présentations de résultats;
* Créer des vidéos explicatives des résultats et des méthodologies pour le partage de connaissances.


 Personnalisation et idéation




* Identifier des opportunités de personnalisation à chaque étape du funnel : page d’accueil, fiches produit, panier et post‑achat;
* Se tenir à jour sur les tendances CRO, UX et personnalisation et agir comme expert interne;
* Identifier les variantes gagnantes comme candidats pour déploiement permanent ou personnalisation.


 Qualifications




* Diplôme dans un domaine quantitatif tel que statistiques, mathématiques, informatique, science des données ou ingénierie;
* 3 à 4 ans d’expérience en tests A/B et CRO en environnement e‑commerce ou produit digital avec impact mesurable sur la conversion;
* Solides bases statistiques : compréhension des p‑values, intervalles de confiance, taille d’échantillon, puissance statistique et biais;
* Expérience avec SiteSpect et Optimizely;
* Capacité à rédiger des tickets Jira clairs et structurés;
* Capacité démontrée à gérer une feuille de route de manière autonome;
* Excellentes compétences en communication pour vulgariser des concepts statistiques;
* Compréhension du front\-end (HTML/CSS) pour la validation QA;
* Expérience avec GA4 ou outils équivalents pour l’analyse de funnel et le suivi des tests;
* Expérience en tests mobile (atout);
* Expérience avec outils de personnalisation (Dynamic Yield, Nosto, Klaviyo) (atout);
* Capacité à créer des maquettes Figma (atout).


 ﻿Description




 Reporting to the Manager, E‑commerce Analytics \& Experimentation, the Analytics Experimentation \& CRO Analyst will own and execute the experimentation program across Groupe Dynamite’s web and mobile app experiences for both Garage and Dynamite brands.




 This role is responsible for defining experimentation strategy, building and prioritizing the test roadmap, launching A/B tests, analyzing results with statistical rigor, and translating insights into measurable conversion and revenue impact. The analyst will collaborate closely with product, development, QA, marketing, and eCommerce stakeholders and serve as the subject matter expert for experimentation and CRO best practices.




 Experimentation Roadmap \& Strategy




* Own and maintain the experimentation roadmap for web and app across both brands, aligned to quarterly conversion and revenue goals;
* Proactively identify incremental improvement opportunities across the full funnel: engagement, product discovery, add\-to\-cart, checkout initiation, and post\-purchase;
* Generate creative, data\-driven hypotheses rooted in UX research, session recordings, funnel analytics, and customer behaviour patterns;
* Prioritise tests using a structured scoring framework and ensure the roadmap reflects the highest\-impact opportunities at all times.


 Test Planning \& Setup




* Write detailed Jira tickets for every experiment including hypothesis, test brief, acceptance criteria, success metrics, audience definition, and edge cases;
* Define primary and guardrail metrics per test and configure audience segments in SiteSpect and Optimizely;
* Implement web tests directly in collaboration with the web developer, and coordinate app test implementations with the development and product teams;
* Maintain a documented, step\-by\-step process for each stakeholder and test type to ensure consistent, repeatable execution.


 Stakeholder Coordination \& Communication




* Run monthly alignment meetings with all relevant stakeholders across product, design, marketing, and brand to maintain roadmap visibility and gather input;
* Manage end\-to\-end communication per test: staging links, implementation updates, QA sign\-off, and go\-live confirmations;
* Keep stakeholders informed of test status, results, and next steps proactively and without being chased.


 QA, UAT \& Launch




* Lead the QA process for every experiment before go\-live, covering device, browser, and edge case scenarios;
* Manage UAT with stakeholders and obtain sign\-off prior to launching;
* Launch tests in SiteSpect and Optimizely and own the go\-live process from start to finish.


 Monitoring, Analysis \& Results




* Monitor live tests continuously and escalate anomalies, traffic drops, or technical issues immediately;
* Own the statistical analysis of results: significance calculations, confidence intervals, segment\-level breakdowns, and revenue impact modelling;
* Declare winners and losers based on statistical significance at a minimum 95% confidence level — never call a test early;
* Produce clear, insight\-driven results documentation in Confluence and results decks for stakeholder review;
* Create video walkthroughs of test results and methodology for asynchronous team knowledge sharing.


 Personalisation \& Creative Ideation




* Identify and propose personalisation opportunities across the funnel: homepage segmentation, PDP experiences, cart interactions, and post\-purchase flows;
* Stay current on CRO, UX, and personalisation trends and serve as the team’s subject matter expert;
* Identify winning test variants as candidates for permanent rollout or personalisation layers across both brands.


 Qualifications




* Degree in a quantitative field such as Statistics, Mathematics, Computer Science, Data Science, or Engineering
* 3 to 4 years of hands\-on A/B testing and CRO experience in an ecommerce or digital product environment, with a clear track record of driving measurable conversion impact;
* Strong statistical foundation: you understand p\-values, confidence intervals, sample size calculation, statistical power, and the risks of peeking and multiple testing — and you apply this rigour consistently;
* Hands\-on experience with both SiteSpect, Optimizely,
* Experience writing Jira tickets that developers, QA, and stakeholders actually want to read — clear hypothesis, defined metrics, precise acceptance criteria;
* Proven ability to own a roadmap and drive it forward independently without day\-to\-day direction;
* Strong communicator able to translate statistical concepts into clear business language for non\-technical audiences;
* Front\-end literacy: comfortable reviewing HTML/CSS implementations and catching issues during QA;
* Experience with GA4 or equivalent analytics platforms for funnel analysis and test monitoring;
* Familiarity with mobile app testing environments and the constraints of in\-app experimentation is an asset;
* Experience with personalisation tools such as Dynamic Yield, Nosto, or Klaviyo segmentation is an asset;
* Ability to create Figma mockups or wireframes to accompany test briefs is an asset.


 Job Type \& Location




 This is a Contract position based out of Mont\-Royal, QC.




 Pay And Benefits




 The pay range for this position is $40\.00 \- $55\.00/hr.




 Workplace Type




 This is a hybrid position in Mont\-Royal,QC.




